135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1031 "The Quotient Rule for Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1033 1474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5220265d-f52d-5c53-952c-690875cf1905" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1031 "Simplifying Square Root Expressions Using the Quotient Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1033 390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6e563fb5-2e53-5b68-a90b-a963f8d0dc96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1031 "Writing Radical Expressions Using Fractional Exponents" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1033 380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6f21843d-1a34-53a0-a3e5-e5b85146fb25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9845" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y = x^5 (\\cos x)^x$. Its derivative is given by\n\n$y'(x) = x^4 (\\cos x)^x \\left(5 + g(x) \\right)$.\n\nFind the function $g(x)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c24da7ef-0070-5aae-bade-c82ea56476ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the function\n\n$$\ny = x^5 (\\cos x)^x\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the natural logarithm of both sides and use the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{5}(\\cos x)^{x}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{5}) + \\ln ((\\cos x)^{x}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= 5\\ln x + x\\ln (\\cos x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(5\\ln x + x\\ln (\\cos x)) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= \\frac{5}{x} + (x)^{′} \\cdot \\ln (\\cos x) + x \\cdot (\\ln (\\cos x))^{′} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= \\frac{5}{x} + \\ln (\\cos x) + x \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos x} \\cdot (-\\sin x) \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= \\frac{5}{x} + \\ln (\\cos x) - x\\tan x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(\\frac{5}{x} + \\ln (\\cos x) - x\\tan x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute\n\n$$\ny = x^5 (\\cos x)^x {:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= x^{5}(\\cos x)^{x}(\\frac{5}{x} + \\ln (\\cos x) - x\\tan x) \\\\\n&= x^{5}(\\cos x)^{x}(\\frac{5}{x} + (x\\ln (\\cos x))/(x) - \\frac{x^{2}\\tan x}{x}) \\\\\n&= x^{4}(\\cos x)^{x}(5 + x ln ⁡ (cos ⁡ x) - x 2 tan ⁡ x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x) = x \\ln (\\cos x) - x^2 \\tan x\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9846" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y = \\dfrac{(x+3)^3}{(x+5)^6}$. The derivative of this function is given by\n$y' = -\\dfrac{g(x)(x+3)^2}{(x+5)^7}$.\n\nFind the function $g(x)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7db11c8c-344b-5d87-a8ae-3b006e5bd92b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the function\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{(x+3)^3}{(x+5)^6}\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln (((x + 3)^{3})/((x + 5)^{6})) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln ((x + 3)^{3}) - \\ln ((x + 5)^{6}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= 3\\ln (x + 3) - 6\\ln (x + 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3\\ln (x + 3) - 6\\ln (x + 5)) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x + 3} - 6 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x + 5} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= \\frac{3}{x + 3} - \\frac{6}{x + 5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(\\frac{3}{x + 3} - \\frac{6}{x + 5})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{(x+3)^3}{(x+5)^6}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= ((x + 3)^{3})/((x + 5)^{6})(\\frac{3}{x + 3} - \\frac{6}{x + 5}) \\\\\n&= ((x + 3)^{3})/((x + 5)^{6})((3(x + 5) - 6(x + 3))/((x + 3)(x + 5))) \\\\\n&= ((x + 3)^{3})/((x + 5)^{6})((-3x - 3)/((x + 3)(x + 5))) \\\\\n&= - (3 (x + 1)(x + 3)^{2})/((x + 5)^{7})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x) = \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{3(x+1)}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y = \\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{x^2}{x^5+ 1}}$. The derivative of this function is given by\n$y' = \\dfrac{g(x)}{3\\sqrt[3]{x(x^5+1)^4}}$.\n\nFind the function $g(x)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0cec84d-96cf-5fed-ba05-a5cfc57841a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1074 "Our function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{5} + 1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}}{\\sqrt[3]{x^{5} + 1}} \\\\\n&= (x^{2/3})/((x^{5} + 1)^{1/3})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln ((x^{2/3})/((x^{5} + 1)^{1/3})) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{2/3}) - \\ln ((x^{5} + 1)^{1/3}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\frac{2}{3}\\ln x - \\frac{1}{3}\\ln (x^{5} + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{2}{3}\\ln x - \\frac{1}{3}\\ln (x^{5} + 1)) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x^{5} + 1} \\cdot (5x^{4}) \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= \\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{5x^{4}}{x^{5} + 1})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{5x^{4}}{x^{5} + 1}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute\n\n$$\ny = \\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{x^2}{x^5+ 1}}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{5} + 1}}(\\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{5x^{4}}{x^{5} + 1}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{5} + 1}}((2(x^{5} + 1) - 5x^{5})/(x(x^{5} + 1))) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{5} + 1}}((-3x^{5} + 2)/(x(x^{5} + 1))) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{5} + 1}}((-3x^{5} + 2)/(\\sqrt[3]{x^{3}(x^{5} + 1)^{3}})) \\\\\n&= (-3 x 5 + 2)/(3\\sqrt[3]{x(x^{5} + 1)^{4}})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x) = \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{-3x^5+2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating a Product" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7613eee3-a281-57cb-bc47-3b1594920bd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating a Quotient" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064310 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "71dd9228-4b05-54d9-aeb2-3bdabf89e0e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating a Radical Expression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064311 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c6005f9a-3eba-5f8d-909d-894d9cd24d12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1045 "Further Logarithmic Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186065206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064435 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4dd7be6e-e9a7-53a7-9076-0bf7c12d09ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065206 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065206 #edb/ref 1061 37035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065206 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "caef414d-4f2a-5504-9b92-39a03d2f3c8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065206 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065207 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065207 #edb/ref 1061 37036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065207 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6a516b4-d0c4-5ec7-8f7e-12edd0e85c51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065207 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065208 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065208 #edb/ref 1061 37037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065208 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "57a60273-bc58-5aff-8dcd-d7139782aa2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065208 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065209 #edb/ref 1061 37038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065209 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8850f22e-33ee-545a-8f5e-4dc37bda3b30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065209 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065210 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065210 #edb/ref 1061 37041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065210 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2141558f-a6d2-515d-902a-620581d72401" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065210 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065396 #edb/ref 1064 "When a function $y=y(x)$ contains complex products, quotients, or radicals, we can use logarithmic differentiation to find the derivative $y'(x)$.\n\nFor example, consider the following function:\n\n$$\ny = x^2 \\cdot 2^x\n$$\n\nOur goal is to find $y'(x)$. To do this, we will use the product rule for logarithms, namely\n\n$$\n\\ln(a b)= \\ln a + \\ln b\n$$\n\nWe differentiate our function by following four steps.\n\n**Step 1.** We take the natural logarithm of both sides and apply the product and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{2} \\cdot 2^{x}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{2}) + \\ln (2^{x}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= 2\\ln x + x\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** Next, we differentiate both sides of our equation using implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(2\\ln x + x\\ln 2) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 2 \\cdot (\\ln x)^{′} + (x)^{′} \\cdot \\ln (2) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + 1 \\cdot \\ln (2) \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= \\frac{2}{x} + \\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Then, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(\\frac{2}{x} + \\ln 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4.** Finally, we substitute back our original expression for\n\n$$\ny =x^2\\cdot 2^x{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= x^{2} \\cdot 2^{x}(\\frac{2}{x} + \\ln 2) \\\\\n&= x \\cdot 2^{x + 1} + x^{2} \\cdot 2^{x}\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065396 #edb/ref 1065 6088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065396 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1895a7f3-5ba4-5a31-85b3-6a7b050b307c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065396 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065397 #edb/ref 1064 "In cases where we wish to differentiate a quotient of functions\n\n$$\ny = f(x) = \\dfrac{g(x)}{h(x)}\n$$\n\nwe can apply the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\ln \\left(\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right) = \\ln a - \\ln b\n$$\n\nFor example, let's compute $y'$, where the function $y$ is given by\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac {e^{x^2}}{(1-2x)^2(x-1)^3}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln ((e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{2}(x - 1)^{3})) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln (e^{x^{2}}) - \\ln ((1 - 2x)^{2}) - \\ln ((x - 1)^{3}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= x^{2} - 2\\ln (1 - 2x) - 3\\ln (x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} - 2\\ln (1 - 2x) - 3\\ln (x - 1)) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 2x - 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - 2x} \\cdot (-2) - 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x - 1} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= 2x + \\frac{4}{1 - 2x} - \\frac{3}{x - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(2x + \\frac{4}{1 - 2x} - \\frac{3}{x - 1})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute our expression for $y$, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{2}(x - 1)^{3})(2x + \\frac{4}{1 - 2x} - \\frac{3}{x - 1}) \\\\\n&= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{2}(x - 1)^{3})((2x(1 - 2x)(x - 1) + 4(x - 1) - 3(1 - 2x))/((1 - 2x)(x - 1))) \\\\\n&= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})(2x(1 - 2x)(x - 1) + 4(x - 1) - 3(1 - 2x)) \\\\\n&= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})(-4x^{3} + 6x^{2} + 8x - 7) \\\\\n&= - (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})(4x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 8x + 7) \\\\\n&= - (e^{x^{2}}(4x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 8x + 7))/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065397 #edb/ref 1065 6090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065397 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8cf6e625-669a-5fda-b756-e1ce091eaa93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065397 #edb/ref 1067 "Using Logarithms to Differentiate a Quotient" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
